    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so when people talk about the \"foundations\" of the modern world, why do you think it's usually framed around the West? like, if you look at places like the Mali Empire or ancient African civilizations, they had huge wealth and complex trade/governance too. are those considered \"secondary\" to the stuff that happened in Europe, or do they just not fit into the same \"civilization\" narrative that the Greeks and Romans started?",
